i don't know if the following is a bug:  i just destroyed the medusa
without being blind.  was on level 25, had located her by monster-
detection spell, was looking around for ways of blinding myself before
heading toward the area where the spell had shown her to be -- when
lo and behold, she shows up in the corridor right next to me (far away
from where i had located her).  i think i had just typed "." in the
turn before she showed up.  i had a mirror, so promptly applied it 
and this took care of her, but what i'm wondering is why i wasn't 
fossilized instantly.  is that something governed by chance, rather 
than a certainty?  or maybe i was speeded, and that gave me a turn 
in which to do something about her before she did something about me --
but that would presuppose an odd view of what it takes for me to _see_
her?  or was it, alas, a bug and thus not a victory i was really
entitled to?  (this was nethack 2.3e.)


